  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14a\"><p><strong>14a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda = (38 \\times 10^{-6})(1.7 \\times 10^{-2}) \\approx 6.46 \\times 10^{-7}\"></span> m</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f = \\frac{c}{\\lambda} = \\frac{3 \\times 10^{8}}{6.46 \\times 10^{-7}} \\approx 4.6 \\times 10^{14}\"></span> Hz <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\approx 460\"></span> THz</p>\n<p>Final answer must be given to 2 significant figures.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14b\"><p><strong>14b</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14c\"><p><strong>14c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>The wavelength of green light is shorter than the wavelength of red light.</p>\n<p>Therefore the first diffraction minimum forms at a smaller angle and the width of the central maximum will decrease.</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Monochromatic red light is incident on a single slit of width <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"38 \\: \\mu\"></span>m and creates a diffraction pattern on a screen behind the slits. The first diffraction minimum forms at an angle of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.70 \\times 10^{-2}\"></span> rad . </p>\n<p>a. Find, in THz, the frequency of the incident light. Give your answer to an appropriate number of significant figures.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>\n<p>b. On the axes, draw how the intensity of the light on the screen varies with the diffraction angle.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>The red light is replaced with green light. </p>\n<p>c. Outline <strong>two</strong> changes to the diffraction pattern.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>"
  },
